        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-08T21:26:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The approach with manual reference counting was used in the legacy implementation likely due to lack of a good library support for smart pointers. With `std::shared_pointer` or `sp` this can actually be made easier. The idea is that whoever needs to hold an instance of `SubmixRoute` uses a strong pointer to it, other users use weak pointers. Once the last strong user will be gone, the instance of `SubmixRoute` will be destroyed automatically, and we can use its destructor to perform any cleanup needed. Weak pointer holders can then check if the object is gone by trying to promote the weak pointer to strong.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "f489df335c57b6d0cebac0ea495c27685e5058fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
